:"POL SCI 6","title":"Introduction to Data Analysis","units":"5","offered":["Fall","Winter","Summer"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Statistics"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three or four hours; discussion, one hour (when scheduled). Not open for credit to students with credit for course 6R. Introduction to collection and analysis of political data, with emphasis on application of statistical reasoning to study of relationships among political variables. Use of computer as aid in analyzing data from various fields of political science, among them comparative politics, international relations, American politics, and public administration. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/POLSCI6"},{"id":"POL SCI 10","title":"Introduction to Political Theory","units":"5","offered":["Fall","Winter","Spring","Summer"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Political Science"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Exposition and analysis of selected political theorists and concepts from Plato to the present. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/POLSCI10"},{"id":"POL SCI 20","title":"World Politics","units":"5","offered":["Fall","Winter","Spring","Summer"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Political Science"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Required of all students concentrating in Field II. Introduction to problems of world politics. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/POLSCI20"},{"id":"POL SCI 30","title":"Politics and Strategy","units":"5","offered":["Fall","Winter","Spring"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Political Science"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three or four hours; discussion, one hour (when scheduled). Introduction to study of strategic interaction in political applications. Use of game theory and other formal modeling strategies to understand politics. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/POLSCI30"},{"id":"POL SCI 40","title":"Introduction to American Politics","units":"5","offered":["Fall","Winter","Spring","Summer"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Political Science"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Basic institutions and processes of democratic politics. Treatment of themes such as constitutionalism, representation, participation, and leadership coupled with particular emphasis on the American case. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/POLSCI40"},{"id":"POL SCI 50","title":"Introduction to Comparative Politics","units":"5","offered":["Fall","Spring","Summer"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Political Science"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Not open for credit to students with credit for course 50R. Comparative study of constitutional principles, governmental institutions, and political processes in selected countries. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/POLSCI50"},{"id":"STATS 10","title":"Introduction to Statistical Reasoning","units":"5","offered":["Fall","Winter","Spring","Summer"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Substitutions"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour; computer laboratory, two hours. Preparation: three years of high school mathematics. Not open for credit to students with credit for course 12, 13, or 15. Introduction to statistical thinking and understanding, including strengths and limitations of basic experimental designs, graphical and numerical summaries of data, inference, regression as descriptive tool. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/STATS10"},{"id":"STATS 12","title":"Introduction to Statistical Methods for Geography and Environmental Studies","units":"5","offered":["Spring"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Substitutions"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, four hours; discussion, one hour; laboratory, one hour. Not open for credit to students with credit for course 10, 11, or 13. Introduction to statistical thinking and understanding, with emphasis on techniques used in geography and environmental science. Underlying logic behind statistical procedures, role of variation in statistical thinking, strengths and limitations of statistical summaries, and fundamental inferential tools. Emphasis on applications in geography and environmental science in laboratory work using professional statistical analysis package, including spatial statistics. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/STATS12"}],"edges":[],"pools":[{"id":"pool-1","label":"The Major","section":"The Major","rule":"at least 10 courses","list_name":null,"courses":["POL SCI 111B","POL SCI 111C","POL SCI M111A","POL SCI 112A","POL SCI M112B","POL SCI 113A","POL SCI 113B","POL SCI 114A","POL SCI 114B","POL SCI 115